 page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>NeoUI v3 MEDIEN and Bluetooth</title><style>:root{color-scheme:dark}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;padding:24px;background:#0d131c;color:#eff6fa;font:15px/1.5 Segoe UI,sans-serif}h1,a,summary{color:#77e7f4}h2{margin-top:32px}p{max-width:1150px}article,.note{background:#17202c;border:1px solid #344454;border-radius:10px;padding:16px;overflow:hidden}.note{border-left:3px solid #77e7f4}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,420px),1fr));gap:18px}.pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px}.pair img{max-width:100%;height:auto}.photo{width:100%;height:300px;object-fit:contain;background:#080d13}select{font:inherit;background:#243b4a;color:#eff6fa;border:1px solid #77e7f4;padding:7px;margin:5px}.player{position:relative;aspect-ratio:2;container-type:inline-size;overflow:hidden;background:#0d131c}.player img{position:absolute;height:auto}.player .bg{inset:0;width:100%;height:100%}.player .card{width:35.15625%;left:60.15625%;top:8.59375%}.player .transport{width:9.375%;top:53.90625%}.prev{left:7.03125%}.pause{left:25.78125%}.next{left:44.53125%}.player .mix,.player .repeat{width:5.625%;left:92.96875%}.mix{top:39.0625%}.repeat{top:51.5625%}.title,.subtitle{position:absolute;left:7%;width:52%;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;white-space:nowrap;text-shadow:0 1px 2px #000}.title{top:18%;font-size:4.2cqw}.subtitle{top:33%;font-size:2.8cqw}.player .source,.player .list,.player .setup{width:6.09375%;top:88.28125%}.source{left:13.28125%}.list{left:46.875%}.setup{left:80.46875%}.barlabels{position:absolute;inset:96% 0 0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);text-align:center;font-size:1.8cqw}.art{position:absolute;left:64.453125%;top:13.4375%;width:28.4375%;aspect-ratio:1;background:repeating-linear-gradient(135deg,#17202c,#17202c 12px,#344454 12px,#344454 24px);display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:2cqw}.art[hidden]{display:none}.art span{padding:8px;background:#0d131ce6}.mode-row{display:flex;gap:15px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap}.mode-row img{background:#0d131c}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:13px}td,th{padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid #344454;text-align:left}summary{cursor:pointer}.scroll{overflow:auto}</style><h1>NeoUI v3 · MEDIEN / BT</h1><p>Eight additional real MCF graphics: BT and generic fallback pairs, shared media source-list states and playlist glyph. Previous 46 changes remain exact. MENU, map, album-art loading and control behavior are preserved.</p><div class="note">These are source-based offline previews, not captured head-unit screens. The player composition uses actual assets with illustrative coordinates and text placement; it does not change HMI layout or hit targets. Blue background is a sample of the traced primary/secondary shader. Source/off names refer to resource variants, not a guessed connection-state mapping. The artwork pattern below is a preview-only sample, not firmware artwork.</div><h2>BT / media source card and transport states</h2><label>Card <select id="card" onchange="update()"><option value="2217">BT source · 2217</option><option value="2202">BT source-off · 2202</option><option value="2214">Generic source / artwork border · 2214</option><option value="2199">Generic source-off · 2199</option><option value="art">Dynamic art sample + real border2214</option></select></label><label>Transport glyph <select id="glyph" onchange="update()"><option value="pause">Pause</option><option value="play">Play</option></select></label><label>Source state slot <select id="slot" onchange="update()">'''+''.join(f'<option value="{i}"'+(' selected' if i==6 else '')+f'>{i}</option>' for i in range(18))+'''</select></label><label>Text <select id="text" onchange="update()"><option value="damaged.-">Photo reference</option><option value="Ein außergewöhnlich langer deutscher Musiktitel">German length sample</option></select></label><div class="grid">'''+player('before')+player('after')+'''</div><p id="stateNote"></p><h2>Shared media source-list button family</h2><p>Array147 → TYPE090 records1131/1133/1134, used by the source-button background script through resourceButtonsMediaType341/342. Native 50 × 94 assets with unchanged alpha and insets; no invented 450px button bitmap.</p><div class="mode-row"><span>v1</span><img id="button_before"><span>v3</span><img id="button_after"></div><h2>Retained renderer-controlled states</h2><p>Shuffle/repeat masks are unchanged. Exact color array8 supplies dim alpha-white, white and green; the samples below multiply those colors into the original glyph. TYPE904 button array204 resolves to no bitmap background. Slider61/39 and indicator917 are unchanged because their state colors are also renderer-controlled. No forced cyan, hidden repeat mark or guessed disabled state.</p><div class="mode-row"><img src="media_bt/mode_956_dim_after.png"><img src="media_bt/mode_956_white_after.png"><img src="media_bt/mode_956_green_after.png"><img src="media_bt/mode_954_white_after.png"><img src="media_bt/mode_953_white_after.png"><img src="media_bt/mode_952_white_after.png"></div><div class="mode-row"><span>Original seekbar track / foreground / indicator</span><img src="media_bt/61_after.png"><img src="media_bt/39_after.png"><img src="media_bt/917_after.png"></div><h2>Eight exact asset changes · v1 / v3</h2><div class="grid">'''+''.join(cards)+'''</div><h2>Eight photo scenarios and scope</h2><div class="grid">'''+''.join(refs)+'''</div><p><a href="VEHICLE_NAV_V3_PREVIEW.html">Vehicle/navigation comparisons</a> · <a href="HOME_SETUP_V3_PREVIEW.html">HOME/SETUP comparisons</a> · <a href="VERIFIED_V3_PREVIEW.html">Transport asset comparisons</a></p><script>const states='''+json.dumps(index)+''';function update(){const slot=document.getElementById('slot').value;const card=document.getElementById('card').value;const glyph=document.getElementById('glyph').value;const s=states[slot];for(const side of ['before','after']){document.getElementById('card_'+side).src='media_bt/'+(card==='art'?'2214':card)+'_'+side+'.png';document.getElementById('art_'+side).hidden=card!=='art';for(const k of ['previous','pause','next'])document.getElementById(k+'_'+side).src='media_bt/'+s[k==='pause'?glyph:k]+'_'+side+'.png';document.getElementById('button_'+side).src='media_bt/'+s.source_button+'_'+side+'.png';}document.querySelectorAll('[data-title]').forEach(e=>e.textContent=document.getElementById('text').value);document.getElementById('stateNote').textContent='State slot '+slot+' · previous '+s.previous+' · '+glyph+' '+s[glyph]+' · next '+s.next+' · source-list button '+s.source_button+'. Positions and state indices are preview controls, not on-device state labels.';}update();</script></html>'''
 (OUT/'neoui_previews/MEDIA_BT_V3_PREVIEW.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf-8');(p/'state_index.json').write_text(json.dumps(index,indent=2),encoding='utf-8');print('PASS: BT/generic/artwork previews, 18 transport/button slots, retained tint samples and eight references')
